In a shop, a certain feloneous orc wizard read all the spellbooks, and
_then_ the blessed scroll of teleportation, and was lucky enough to find
the stairs down before the Kops caught up.  By chance, those stairs went
down into a mine.

Still low level, he's wandering around second level mines or so, with
this huge entourage of pet gnomes, dwarves, jackels, a kobold lord, and
such.  The intelligent monsters helpfully start dropping what they're
carrying in case I'd like to add it to _my_ trove.

I'm sure if he lives long enough I'll find out why this is a bad idea,
but charm monster seems like a way out of proportion spell to be cast
with zero failure for a low level wizard; I can see a new conduct
challenge: a pet of every species alive at once.

Ferrying this crew from level to level is "interesting", so the problem
may be self limiting, but still????

